## Project layout (clean architecture)

```
src/{{ project_slug }}/
├── main.py              # app factory: routers, error handlers, lifespan
├── core/                # settings, logging, database config
├── domain/              # entities, repository interfaces, business errors (no framework code)
├── application/         # services (use cases) that orchestrate the domain
├── infrastructure/      # SQLAlchemy models, sessions, repository implementations
└── presentation/api/    # routers, request/response schemas, dependency wiring
```

Dependencies point inward: `presentation` → `application` → `domain`, and `infrastructure`
implements the interfaces declared in `domain`.

### Adding a feature
1. `domain/<feature>/`: entity, repository interface, errors
2. `application/<feature>/`: service + DTOs
3. `infrastructure/<feature>/`: ORM model + repository; import the model in `infrastructure/db/models.py`
4. `presentation/api/v1/`: schemas + router; register it in `v1/router.py`; wire deps in `deps.py`
{%- if migrations == "alembic" %}
5. `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add <feature>"` and review the migration

## Migrations

```bash
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run alembic downgrade -1
```
